.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "BSDSF24A012-OS-A01" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words, and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.B int wordCount(FILE *file, int *lines, int *words, int *chars);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wordCount
reads
.I file
from its current position and stores the number of newline characters, words,
and characters in the locations supplied by
.IR lines ,
.IR words ,
and
.IR chars .
The file position is advanced to end-of-file.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or -1 if an argument is NULL or a read error occurs.
